`ifndef HI3520V100_IO_CONFIG_RDL
`define HI3520V100_IO_CONFIG_RDL

regfile eIO_CONFIG {
    name = "IO configuration (pin multiplexing control), Hi3520 V100";
    desc = "
    Pin multiplexing control registers of the Hi3520 V100 at 0x200F0000 ('IO config 寄存器', 64 KB window, DS Table 1-1 line 11535): 83 registers `reg0`..`reg82` at offsets 0x0..0x148,
    one register per software-multiplexed pin, each holding one RW field (1 or 2 bits) that selects the pin function; all reset to 0 (the first listed
    function, usually the pin's primary function, GPIO where the pin is GPIO by default). The register name is the data sheet's; the register title names the pin.

    Source: Hi3520 用户指南 (user guide / data sheet), original Chinese edition 文档版本 02 (2010-01-19), section 2.4 (summary Table 2-35, dump line 5094) and section 2.5 (register descriptions, dump lines 5305..7785). Chinese original, so the
    values are high confidence; the function names are copied verbatim, the sentences translated. No Hi3520 V100 vendor code (U-Boot/kernel board files) exists in this
    workspace to cross-check against (only Hi3520D and Hi3516A trees), so the register set is data-sheet only.

    | Register | Offset | Pin | Values |
    |----------|--------|-----|--------|
    | reg0 | 0x0 | VI0HS | 00=VI0HS, 01=URXD2, 10=GPIO1_3 |
    | reg1 | 0x4 | VI0VS | 00=VI0VS, 01=UTXD2, 10=GPIO1_4 |
    | reg2 | 0x8 | VI0DAT0 | 0=VI0DAT0, 1=VOUDAT8 |
    | reg3 | 0xC | VI0DAT1 | 0=VI0DAT1, 1=VOUDAT9 |
    | reg4 | 0x10 | VI0DAT2 | 0=VI0DAT2, 1=VOUDAT10 |
    | reg5 | 0x14 | VI0DAT3 | 0=VI0DAT3, 1=VOUDAT11 |
    | reg6 | 0x18 | VI0DAT4 | 0=VI0DAT4, 1=VOUDAT12 |
    | reg7 | 0x1C | VI0DAT5 | 0=VI0DAT5, 1=VOUDAT13 |
    | reg8 | 0x20 | VI0DAT6 | 0=VI0DAT6, 1=VOUDAT14 |
    | reg9 | 0x24 | VI0DAT7 | 0=VI0DAT7, 1=VOUDAT15 |
    | reg10 | 0x28 | VI1DAT0 | 00=VI1DAT0, 01=GPIO4_0, 10=VOUDAT0 |
    | reg11 | 0x2C | VI1DAT1 | 00=VI1DAT1, 01=GPIO4_1, 10=VOUDAT1 |
    | reg12 | 0x30 | VI1DAT2 | 00=VI1DAT2, 01=GPIO4_2, 10=VOUDAT2 |
    | reg13 | 0x34 | VI1DAT3 | 00=VI1DAT3, 01=GPIO4_3, 10=VOUDAT3 |
